","A few streets of a grubby district have been 'restored' to their condition in the post-Korean War 1960s, with wooden lamppost and bronze figures illustrating scenes of hardscrabble street life. Also easy walking distance to Yongdusan Park."],["BIFF Square","sight",35.1011,129.0279,"Nampo-dong, Jung-gu","24 hours (hours vary by store)","","","","r","As a symbolic location for the Busan International Film Festival, BIFF Square features handprints of famous film directors and actors. Once a district with a high concentration of theaters, it is now a representative street food…"],["Chinatown","sight",35.11476,129.03898,"","","","","","r","Home of Busan's Chinese community with cheap and delicious dumplings, though most of the Chinese have left the area, and it is today mainly home to Russians."],["Ibagu-gil and 168 Steps","sight",35.11662,129.03682,"","","","","","r","This is an example of old, steep residential area of Busan that was formed after Korean War. Although you can walk the famous 168 steps, there is a free monorail that takes you uphill."],["Busan Port Boat Tour","activity",35.10482,129.03864,"Jungang","","","","","r","If you are interested in the industrial side of Busan then the Port tour is hard to beat. Passengers on board can see the port facilities of Busan Port, including the passenger terminal, general piers, and container terminals. You will…"],["Busan City Tour","activity",35.1155,129.03973,"","","","","","r","All-day ticket available for double decker tour buses."],["Leegane Tteokbokki","restaurant",35.10075,129.0251,"48, Bupyeong 1-gil, Jung-gu","10:00-17:00","","","","r","Tteokbokki restaurant is inside the can market. Prices are reasonable at ₩5,000 for tteokbokki, ₩5,000 for fries, and ₩1,000 for a corn dog."],["Lee Jae Mo Pizza, Busan","restaurant",35.10211,129.0306,"31 Gwangbokjungang-ro, Jung-gu","11:00-21:30","","","","r","This is the most famous pizza restaurant in Central Busan. On weekdays and weekends, a very large number of people line up to eat inside the restaurant. To solve this problem, a take-out only store has been opened across the street.…"],["Kkangdwaehu","restaurant",35.10203,129.02582,"57 Bupyeong 1-gil, Jung-gu","12:00-22:30","","","","r","This is a pork cutlet version of the Korean fried chicken called 'Pork Ribs Fried'. It is available in large, medium, and small sizes, with prices ranging from ₩13,000 to ₩23,000 depending on the size."],["Donghwa Chinese Restaurant","restaurant",35.10579,129.02347,"73-8 Bosu-dong 2(i)-ga, Jung-gu","11:30-20:30","","","","r","This Chinese restaurant in Busan, Jung-gu, is famous for its yuni-jjajang and sweet and sour pork. Noodles and fried rice are inexpensive at ₩6,000-8,000, but other dishes cost ₩20,000-30,000. Closed every Wednesday."],["Dolswe Wood-fired grilling","restaurant",35.10075,129.0251,"19-1 Haegwan-ro, Jung-gu","16:30-21:40","","","","r","A Korean barbecue restaurant with a single menu item: beef outside skirt It costs ₩13,000 per bowl and has sides such as Doenjangjjigae, rice, and Naengmyeon. Closed every Sunday and last order is at 21:00."],["Bosu-dong Book Street","sight",35.10184,129.02322,"8-1 Bosu-dong 1-ga, Jung-gu, Busan","","","","","r","A historic alley filled with secondhand bookstores, some of which have been around for generations. It’s a nostalgic and peaceful place for book lovers."],["Haksun Milmyeon","restaurant",35.1051,129.0201,"549, Daesin-ro, Seo-gu","10:00-20:00 (Break time 15:30-16:30)","","","","r","Offers milmyeon (wheat noodles), a regional food item. Both cold noodles (mul milmyeon) and spicy mixed noodles (bibim milmyeon) are available."]]}